            <ArticleTitle>An unusual etiology of chest pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>352-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Absence of right coronary artery is a rare coronary anomaly that may present with myocardial ischemia. This is a case report of a 49-year-old female with chest pain and positive stress test. Coronary angiogram revealed absence of right coronary artery with normal left coronary system.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
